# Swagger / OpenAPI required for every API endpoint

Every HTTP API endpoint **must** appear in Swagger UI at `/docs` (OpenAPI at `/openapi.json`, ReDoc at `/redoc`).

## Mandatory on each route decorator

- `summary` — short English title
- `description` — what it does, side effects, CAG/LLM notes if any
- `tags` — must match a tag in `app.main.OPENAPI_TAGS`
- `response_model` — Pydantic model (never a bare `dict` for JSON APIs)
- `status_code` — explicit success status
- `responses` — document success **and** relevant errors (422, 502, …) with models
- `response_description` — one-line success description

## Mandatory on request/response schemas

- Pydantic models in `app/schemas/`
- `Field(description=...)` on every public field
- Examples via `json_schema_extra` and/or `openapi_examples` so Swagger “Try it out” works
- Validation constraints reflected in the schema (`min_length`, `ge`, …)

## App-level OpenAPI

- Keep `docs_url="/docs"`, `redoc_url="/redoc"`, `openapi_url="/openapi.json"` enabled
- Set `title`, `summary`/`description`, `version`, `openapi_tags`
- English only (see `english-code.mdc`)

## Checklist before merging a new endpoint

1. Visible under `/docs`
2. Try-it-out request example works
3. Documented error responses match real behavior
4. No `include_in_schema=False` unless the route is explicitly internal/non-API

## Do not

- Undocumented routes
- Hide public API with `include_in_schema=False`
- Disable `/docs` in normal/development builds
- Spanish OpenAPI text
